Below is an interactive rendering of a set $\manifold \subseteq \bbR^3$ which is a $2$-manifold.
As you move your mouse around $\manifold$ in the first figure, the hovered point $\point \in \manifold$ is associated with a chart $(\open, \chart)$ which is also rendered.
The second figure shows the coordinate domain identification $\chart(\open) \subseteq\bbR^2$ and the coordinate $\chart(\point) \in \bbR^2$.
As you move your mouse around over $\chart(\open) \subseteq \bbR^2$, you can see its homeomorphic identification with $\open \subseteq \manifold$.

<ManifoldCharts />

<small>
  (Note that if you hold down the right mouse button over the first figure, the chart won't change; this helps you have a view of the chart while you are interacting with the second figure).
  </small>
